# Hosts that block automated requests but work fine in a browser.
# Each was verified by hand on 2026-08-25; they are not dead links, they are
# publishers that refuse bots. Re-verify manually once a term.

# ACM Digital Library — 403 to any non-browser client
dl\.acm\.org

# MIT Press — 403 to bots; Auditing AI is genuinely open access
mitpress\.mit\.edu
direct\.mit\.edu

# Elsevier — 400 to bots
sciencedirect\.com

# NYT — paywalled and bot-blocked; marked `access: paywalled` in resources.yml
nytimes\.com

# Amazon — aggressive bot detection, and these are stable ASIN links
amazon\.com

# LinkedIn / X and similar walled platforms, should any reading ever cite one
linkedin\.com

# Verified by hand on 2026-09-03. Same story as the publishers above: these
# answer a browser and refuse a bot.

# Anthropic and OpenAI product pages — 403 to non-browser clients
claude\.ai
platform\.openai\.com

# DeepLearning.AI — 403 to bots; the short course is genuinely free
deeplearning\.ai

# Lecture-deck media is generated at deploy time and never committed, so the
# links on the Slides page resolve in the built site and not in a bare checkout.
# The link checker runs against the checkout, so it can only ever see them
# missing -- see ADR-019 for why the media is not in the repository.
docs/slides/media/
